Feather Mail is a modern, developer-friendly SMTP mail server framework built
on Elixir and the BEAM runtime. It exposes a clean, pluggable pipeline of
adapters for authentication, access control, routing, delivery, spam
filtering, and logging, letting you assemble a mail server (MSA/MTA) that fits
your deployment without wrestling with legacy mail-server complexity.

Feather is distributed as a self-contained Erlang/OTP release (the runtime is
bundled), configured through two Elixir config files (server.exs and
pipeline.exs).
